OL,3,GNEWSANoisy vehicle checks planned for
OL,4,AOctober
OL,5,
OL,6,FRoadside checks on noisy Guernsey
OL,7,Fvehicles are expected to begin in
OL,8,FOctober, according to a leading island
OL,9,Fpolitician.
OL,11,FDeputy Adrian Gabriel, president of
OL,12,FGuernsey's Environment and
OL,13,FInfrastructure Committee, said the
OL,14,Fpilot scheme had been held up because
OL,15,Fcivil servants did not have the power
OL,16,Fto stop vehicles and had to work
OL,17,Falongside police officers.
OL,19,FThe States agreed last year to
OL,20,Fintroduce a decibel limit for vehicle
OL,21,Fexhausts, but a trial is needed before
OL,22,Fthe new law can be brought into force.
OL,23,APub: 12-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Ch Is NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
